  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nModel guidance shows upper-lvl ridging migrating over the Four \nCorners region by this weekend with 500 mb hght fields increasing to \naround 588-590 dam. As this occurs, global models show a weak upper- \nlow developing over N MX and far W TX which will induce easterly \nflow aloft over our forecast area. The increased pressure gradient \nbetween both features will bring breezy conditions to southeastern \nand southcentral AZ from Saturday through Monday. Elevated winds \nwill likely develop each morning and persist into the early \nafternoon with gusts reaching 30-35 mph over the high terrain and 20-\n 25 mph across the lower deserts. This sfc easterly flow will help \nkeep high temperatures near normal across southcentral AZ, but \novernight lows will be elevated in the low to mid 70s. The 500 mb \nridge axis looks to shift back to the over SoCal and the Great Basin \nearly next week as a weak trough passes through the Intermountain \nWest. This pattern should maintain temperatures in a near normal \nrange across central and eastern portions of the region, but allow \nhighs to warm around 3-5 degrees above normal across the western \ndeserts where highs will likely reach the low 100s each afternoon.",
